Is it true that you lose luck when you save a game of nethack?!  That
seem extremely stupid to me...I realize that if you save you can
cheat by backing up your save files, but some games can last a very
long time.  Does it make sense to penalize someone for not being able
to sit at the computer for 30 hours straight?

Look at it this way...on Unix systems players can be kept from having
access to their save files.  On a PC, if someone wants to cheat, is
that really such a big deal?  Zork has built-in cheating of that very
nature!  I don't see why nethack has to be so moralistic, especially
at such a high price!


